From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: stage Cliffs two-pipe NoC lifecycle and platform data

Adapt Qualcomm Iris33_2P logic from OnePlus SM7675 commit
1138e00fee63582a0cc6a53af3286621786827b7, variant/iris33 and platform/cliffs.
Cross-check the preset table and key quiesce offsets/retry limits against
the exact Uke OS3.0.304.0 msm_video.ko (private SHA256
2976535e5523521d953bdc762fc446e02bd5b564b28db34789d066b6070406df).

Keep existing platforms unchanged. Add a specific preset hook, masked
Cliffs QoS setup, two-pipe NoC error registers, bounded LPI/sideband
quiesce and a separate ops/platform table. Do not reset bridges when
idle or sideband polling times out. The wrapper retains the native
forced-shutdown policy; fault recovery remains unqualified.

No Iris OF match or DT enablement is added. The exact private VPU
filename is selected, but PAS trust, firmware mmap/device regions,
regulator/genpd/OPP ownership and controller retention remain open.
This is source-only preparation; no build or hardware pass is claimed.

